# Generated figures
# Plots are derived artifacts — regenerate them from the tracked .csv rather
# than storing them. The run plots under output/ are handled by output/.gitignore,
# which is deny-all and simply stops re-including *.png; this rule covers
# everywhere else. docs/ images are hand-written documentation, so keep those.
# Adding a genuinely new figure elsewhere needs `git add -f`.
*.png
!docs/*.png

# Real-robot deployment binaries (handover_sim2real/sim2real/)
# The sim2real SOURCE is tracked — policy_runner.py, camera.py, the calibration
# scripts and their small .npy/.json. These are the payloads that came with it:
# 454 MB of .ckpt, 630 MB of RealSense .bag, 15 MB of rendered .mp4. GitHub
# hard-rejects anything over 100 MB, and git keeps blobs forever, so a later
# delete would not shrink the history.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: checkpoint/*/config.yaml and normalization.npz.
# Those are ~1 KB and are the ONLY record of how to denormalize a checkpoint's
# output — same reasoning as the run npz under output/.gitignore.
*.ckpt
*.bag
*.mp4
# WEIGHTS, ANYWHERE — not just under sim2real/checkpoint/. That path-anchored
# rule is why a 149 MB SAM2 checkpoint reached the index: a bad cwd created a
# duplicate package tree at sim2real/handover_sim2real/sim2real/checkpoint/sam2/,
# which has an extra `handover_sim2real/sim2real/` in the middle and so matched
# nothing. An unanchored rule cannot be dodged by where the file lands, and a
# binary that size is effectively permanent — deleting it in a later commit
# leaves it in history and every clone still pays for it.
#
# The small files BESIDE a checkpoint stay tracked (config.yaml,
# normalization.npz, README.md, source.txt): the payload does not carry the
# Normalizer and the .h5 it was fitted on lives on /scratch, so those are the
# only record of how to denormalize a policy's output.
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# Real-robot SESSION RECORDINGS (handover_sim2real/sim2real/output/).
# `exp_recorder.py` writes one directory per run of the rig, holding a raw dump
# per attempt: the policy's input cloud and action as flat float arrays, the
# tripod depth frame as uint16, plus the per-attempt json/csv/jsonl around them.
# Measured at 2.4 GB across 601 files for 17 sessions — larger than everything
# else in this repository combined, and it grows by ~140 MB every time the rig
# is run.
#
# NOT DERIVED, AND STILL NOT TRACKED. Unlike curves.png these cannot be
# regenerated — the robot moved once. They are primary data, and that is an
# argument for BACKING THEM UP, not for putting them in git: blobs are permanent,
# so a session committed today is paid for by every clone forever, and a later
# `git rm` does not shrink the history. Sync them the way the .h5 shards are
# synced.
#
# THE SESSION DIRECTORIES, NOT THE FOLDER THEY SIT IN. Two hand-authored results
# sheets live loose in real_experiments/ among the dumps — `Thesis -
# Experiments - Regrasp - filled.csv` and `results_subject1_right.csv`, 1.3 KB,
# written by a person rather than by the recorder and not reproducible from
# anything. A blanket rule on the folder swept those out along with 2.4 GB of
# arrays they have nothing in common with, so only the dated session dirs one
# level down are ignored and anything loose in real_experiments/ stays tracked.
handover_sim2real/sim2real/output/*
!handover_sim2real/sim2real/output/real_experiments/
handover_sim2real/sim2real/output/real_experiments/*/

# The recorder's raw array dumps, UNANCHORED — same lesson as the weights rule
# above. A path-anchored pattern is dodged the moment a session is written from
# a different cwd, and these are exactly the files that must never land in a
# commit by accident.
*.f4
*.f8
*.u16

# Per-iteration copies inside a DEPLOYMENT bundle
# (handover_sim2real/sim2real/checkpoint/<run>/iter_NN/).
# `output/.gitignore` already worked this out for output/dagger_runs/*/iters/
# and the same argument applies verbatim here, because the deploy script copies
# the whole run: 26 iterations x {config.yaml, log.csv, normalization.npz} = 78
# of the 90 files in a bundle, against the 12 that are the bundle.
#
# A normalizer is only worth keeping next to the checkpoint it denormalizes, and
# the ONLY checkpoints a bundle carries are best/ and last/ — the per-iteration
# .pt were never copied and never tracked, so these 78 normalize nothing. The
# per-iter log.csv is epoch-level detail already summarised one row per
# iteration in the bundle's own dagger_log.csv.
#
# What stays: README.md, config.yaml, command_axes.json, dagger_log.csv, and
# best/ and last/ complete with their config.yaml, normalization.npz and
# source.txt. That handful IS the deployment record — it is what the robot
# loads and what says which run it came from.
handover_sim2real/sim2real/checkpoint/*/iter_*/

# The stray duplicate package tree itself. It holds nothing but the checkpoint
# above; the real tree is at the repo root.
handover_sim2real/sim2real/handover_sim2real/

# SLURM job output. `*.log` near the top of this file does not match .out/.err.
slurm_logs/
*.out
*.err

output_home_shards/
